--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS INSIDE PDFIUM
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

PDFium is not a single-licence work. Its source tree incorporates a number of
third-party libraries — among them FreeType, libjpeg-turbo, libopenjpeg, libpng,
zlib, and Google's own Skia and Abseil — each under its own licence, several of
which carry their own attribution requirements.

A binary built from PDFium therefore contains code under those licences, and
distributing it means honouring them. This repository does not vendor PDFium's
source, so the authoritative list is not reproduced here: it is the LICENSE file
and the third_party/ directory of the PDFium checkout the build fetches, at the
revision recorded by your build. Consult those before redistributing a binary.

If you need a self-contained notice file for a product, generate it from the
PDFium checkout your build produced rather than copying this file — only that
checkout knows which components and versions actually went in.

This summary is a pointer, not legal advice.
